# --------------------- gwf tvkg options ---------------------
# flopy subpackage tvkg_filerecord tvkg k tvkg_k
# flopy parent_name_type parent_package MFPackage

block options
name readarraygrid
type keyword
reader urword
optional false
longname use array-based grid input
description indicates that array-based grid input will be used for the time-varying hydraulic conductivity (TVKG) package.  This keyword must be specified to use array-based grid input.
default_value true

block options
name print_input
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print input to listing file
description keyword to indicate that information for each change to the hydraulic conductivity in a cell will be written to the model listing file.

block options
name tas_filerecord
type record tas6 filein tas6_filename
shape
reader urword
tagged true
optional true
longname
description

block options
name tas6
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname time-array series keyword
description keyword to specify that record corresponds to a time-array-series file.

block options
name filein
type keyword
shape
in_record true
reader urword
tagged true
optional false
longname file keyword
description keyword to specify that an input filename is expected next.

block options
name tas6_filename
type string
preserve_case true
in_record true
reader urword
optional false
tagged false
longname file name of time series information
description defines a time-array-series file defining a time-array series that can be used to assign time-varying values. See the ``Time-Variable Input'' section for instructions on using the time-array series capability.

block options
name export_array_netcdf
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
mf6internal export_nc
longname export array variables to netcdf output files.
description keyword that specifies input gridded arrays should be written to the model output NetCDF file with attributes that support using the generated file as a MODFLOW 6 simulation input.  This option only has an effect when an output model NetCDF file is configured and the simulation is run in VALIDATE mode, otherwise it is ignored.
extended true

# --------------------- gwf tvkg period ---------------------

block period
name iper
type integer
block_variable true
in_record true
tagged false
shape
valid
reader urword
optional false
longname stress period number
description REPLACE iper {}

block period
name k
type double precision
shape (nodes)
reader readarray
time_series true
layered true
netcdf true
optional true
longname hydraulic conductivity (L/T)
description is the new hydraulic conductivity, as per K in the NPF package, for each cell from the start of the specified stress period.  A cell with the DNODATA value (3.0E+30) is unchanged.  The k array may be defined by a time-array series (see the ``Using Time-Array Series in a Package'' section).
default_value 3.e30

block period
name k22
type double precision
shape (nodes)
reader readarray
time_series true
layered true
netcdf true
optional true
longname hydraulic conductivity of second ellipsoid axis (L/T)
description is the new hydraulic conductivity of the second ellipsoid axis (or the ratio of K22/K if the K22OVERK NPF package option is specified), as per K22 in the NPF package, for each cell from the start of the specified stress period.  A cell with the DNODATA value (3.0E+30) is unchanged.  The k22 array may be defined by a time-array series.  A ratio is applied to the cell's K when it is given or, for a time-array series, at each time step.  A ratio cannot be read from NetCDF input.
default_value 3.e30

block period
name k33
type double precision
shape (nodes)
reader readarray
time_series true
layered true
netcdf true
optional true
longname hydraulic conductivity of third ellipsoid axis (L/T)
description is the new hydraulic conductivity of the third ellipsoid axis (or the ratio of K33/K if the K33OVERK NPF package option is specified), as per K33 in the NPF package, for each cell from the start of the specified stress period.  A cell with the DNODATA value (3.0E+30) is unchanged.  The k33 array may be defined by a time-array series.  A ratio is applied to the cell's K when it is given or, for a time-array series, at each time step.  A ratio cannot be read from NetCDF input.
default_value 3.e30
